 same local/external function inventory as list_strings and list_procedures. They do not establish discovery of undefined strings or unidentified functions.","Ghidra (ghidra 12.2) read_binary_inventory_summary: Default-space addresses use lowercase 0x-prefixed hexadecimal; other address spaces use <percent-encoded-space>:0x<hex>.","Ghidra (ghidra 12.2) read_binary_inventory_summary: Ghidra Program checkpoint mode is disabled: closing discards metadata edits; original executable bytes are unchanged. For stock ELF/PE/Mach-O on Linux/macOS, set REA_GHIDRA_CHECKPOINT_DIR to a private absolute directory before starting REA (restart MCP after changing its startup environment).","Ghidra (ghidra 12.2) read_binary_inventory_summary: Known provider defect ghidra-10154 (jump-table-unrecovered-function-truncated): Ghidra 12.2 leaves an aarch64 switch unrecovered when it is a byte-offset bounded by and-0xff. The function body stops at the indirect branch. Upstream issue https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/10154 is open and names a Swift -O swift-enum switch; it has no fix commit and no milestone. REA reproduced the unrecovered jump table on the exact 12.2 build with an AArch64 ELF object of that instruction shape. A compare-bounded byte table still recovers. This record stays on every admitted build until a release is known to clear it.","Ghidra (ghidra 12.2) read_binary_inventory_summary: Known provider defect ghidra-9996 (jump-table-flow-references-omitted): Ghidra 12.2 can omit jump-table flow references and emit incorrect decompiler output for clang -O0 x86-64 switches whose case labels start above zero. Upstream issue https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/9996 is closed by c93917a622211349998f641de54cfdbe0e0e5bee, milestone 12.2.1, which is not yet released. This limitation is recorded for parsed 12.2 releases whose patch is below 12.2.1, including a zero patch and a suffix, and clears on 12.2.1. REA's verified switch lane compiles with